Restart Tokri on the computer hosting the app

1. Open a terminal in this repository.
2. Stop the running app with Ctrl+C.
3. Pull the latest code and start the app:

   git pull --ff-only
   .venv/bin/python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload

If Git reports conflicting local changes, preserve and resolve them before
continuing. Do not discard local work.

Keep the existing public tunnel running. On your other device, open the
public dashboard URL and refresh the page. If you restarted the tunnel,
use the new URL it prints.

Refreshing the browser does not pull new code from GitHub. The hosting
computer must pull the latest code first. Restart the app after backend
or .env changes.

Checking payment SMS

Open <your-dashboard-url>/api/payment-status to check the configuration on
the computer actually hosting the dashboard. This never exposes API keys.
MOCK_CASHFREE=1 generates fake links and sends no SMS. For real Cashfree
requests, configure these in the hosting computer's private .env:

   MOCK_CASHFREE=0
   CASHFREE_APP_ID=<your Cashfree app ID>
   CASHFREE_SECRET=<your Cashfree secret>
   CASHFREE_ENV=sandbox

Use credentials for the selected environment. Never commit the private
.env. Restart BOTH the dashboard process and the separate MCP server after
changing these settings: Sarvam calls the MCP server, which loads its own
configuration. Restart it using its existing MCP_ALLOWED_HOST value:

   MCP_ALLOWED_HOST=<your-existing-MCP-hostname> .venv-mcp/bin/python -m app.mcp_server

The SMS goes to the customer's saved number. Cashfree accepting a request
does not confirm delivery to the phone. Do not switch to production just
to test SMS; production links can collect real payments.

Payment records in Cashfree

New order links include the Tokri order ID, order total, amount due now,
wallet contribution, and outstanding balance in Cashfree's link notes.
Cashfree collects only the amount due after the wallet contribution.

POST /payment/sync with JSON {"order_id": <Tokri order ID>} to fetch the
existing link's status from Cashfree and reconcile the local order. Include
the same X-Tokri-Secret header used for the voice tools. Orders are confirmed
only for matching, fully paid INR links. Cashfree's signed webhook continues
to confirm paid links automatically when PUBLIC_BASE_URL is configured and
reachable. The sync endpoint is a fallback if the webhook was missed.

Vercel dashboard with the backend running on your computer

This repository uses FastAPI and plain HTML, not Vite. The Vercel entry
point accepts API_URL, or VITE_API_URL for compatibility, as a server-side
gateway setting. API_URL takes precedence if both are set.

1. On your backend computer, run the app as usual:

   .venv/bin/python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload

2. Keep your existing HTTPS tunnel to that app running. If you need one:

   cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:8000

3. In the Vercel project's environment variables, set:

   VITE_API_URL=https://<your-backend-tunnel-hostname>

   Select the environments you use (Production and/or Preview), save the
   variable, and redeploy. Import this repository from its root with the
   FastAPI framework preset. Leave Vite build/output overrides unset.

4. Open https://<your-vercel-hostname>/deployment-health to check gateway
   configuration, and /health to check that the backend is reachable.

The correct local URL is http://127.0.0.1:8000, not http://127.0.0.1.8000.
A loopback URL works only on the same computer. Vercel requires the public
HTTPS tunnel URL. Do not use the Vercel dashboard's own URL as API_URL.
When a temporary tunnel URL changes, update Vercel's variable and redeploy.

The gateway forwards the dashboard, API, media, authentication, and Cashfree
webhooks to the same backend. Keep the backend computer and tunnel running.
Cashfree and Sarvam credentials stay in that backend's private .env. This
keeps SQLite and audio storage on the backend instead of Vercel's temporary
function filesystem. The separate MCP server and its existing tunnel still
need to be running for Sarvam voice calls.
